    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32217" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">octōnārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		octoni, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>consisting of eight</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">numerus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 9, § 86</span></i>
			 Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">versus,</span>”
				<i>an Iambic verse of eight feet</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 4, 72</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Diom. p. 514</span></i> P.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fistula,</span>”
				<i>the plate for which was eight inches broad</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Front. Aquaed. 28</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 31, 6,
				31, § 58</span></i>.</div>
